Third-party components
----------------------

fury-shared (tools/fury-config depends on it; linked into the fury-config helper)
  https://github.com/furyteamtop/fury-antidetect-browser, directory shared-rs
  Copyright The Fury Authors. License: AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  Pinned to commit 2c572eb0a02939e01c3992870c9ca84f93145348 (release v0.3.5).
  Its persona catalogue data (directory shared/) is Apache-2.0.

Fury core (downloaded at runtime, never redistributed by AnyProfile)
  https://github.com/furyteamtop/fury-antidetect-browser/releases
  A patched Chromium. Fury's patches: BSD-3-Clause. Chromium: BSD-3-Clause and
  the licenses of its third-party components. AnyProfile downloads the
  notarized release, verifies its SHA-256 and Apple signature, and executes it
  unmodified.

Widevine CDM
  Not shipped. When Google Chrome is installed, AnyProfile copies the user's own
  licensed CDM from the Chrome bundle into each profile on that same machine,
  as the Fury agent does.

AliasMode design tokens
  frontend/src/styles/tokens.css adapts the palette, type scale and elevation
  recipe of the AliasMode dashboard (https://github.com/aliasmode/aliasmode,
  web/styles.css, commit 56c18f9). Copyright AliasMode authors.
  License: Apache-2.0. No AliasMode source code is included.

Inter typeface
  Bundled through @fontsource-variable/inter. Copyright The Inter Project
  Authors. License: SIL Open Font License 1.1.

Go, npm and Rust dependencies are listed in go.mod, frontend/package-lock.json
and tools/fury-config/Cargo.lock, each under its own license.

tools/bench/*.mjs were written for this project during the engine evaluation
(October 2026) and are licensed like the rest of the repository.
